    {
        "content": "<p>like, afaik there's no bundled version, so strictly speaking your answer would be \"no\", but the fact that you're asking for a bundled version seems strange because afaik it usually doesn't matter too much whether your objects are or aren't bundled? so i'm curious what setup you're in where it becomes more ergonomic to have a bundled version.</p>",
        "id": 586180531,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1776445861
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm trying to define something like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">The span chain of an ordered family of vectors is the set of spans of initial segments.</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">For `ι = Fin n`:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">Given a finite ordered list of vectors `v₀, v₁, v₂, ..., vₙ`, the span chain of v is the set</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">`{{0}, span(v₀), span(v₀, v₁), ..., span(v₀, v₁, ..., vₙ)}`.</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">For `ι = ℕ`:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">Given a countable sequence of vectors `v₀, v₁, v₂, ...`, the span chain of v is the set</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">`{{0}, span(v₀), span(v₀, v₁), ..., span(v₀, v₁, v₂, ...)}`.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">This includes the spans of every finite initial list of vectors as well as the span of the entire</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">sequence. In the case that `M` is a Hilbert space and `v₀, v₁, v₂, ...` is a Schauder basis, then</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">taking the closure of every element in the span chain produces a nest.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">spanChain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">span</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">''</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LowerSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(span chain is not a standard name, as far as I am aware). This is for <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"217875\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Singular.20Value.20Decomposition/with/586083836\">#Is there code for X? &gt; Singular Value Decomposition</a> and <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"287929\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Chains.2C.20flags.2C.20and.20filtrations/with/581533718\">#mathlib4 &gt; Chains, flags, and filtrations</a>. Basically, I'm trying to figure out if the return type should be <code>Set</code>, <code>Sublattice</code>, or something else.</p>\n<p>I agree that bundled instances don't really matter most of the time but I also think that if there happens to already be a bundled version then it makes sense to take advantage of it.</p>",
        "id": 586246705,
        "sender_full_name": "Niels Voss",
        "timestamp": 1776484506
    }
